Brief 18 Step 2 — the missing post-exam fixture, for docs/Spec/.

docs/Spec/ is the locked canonical corpus and is read-only to Claude Code
(.claude/hooks/block-spec-and-secrets.mjs hard-blocks the write), so this is
handed over as a patch rather than committed.

  git apply docs/plans/calendar_fixture_post_sitting_interval.patch

Adds one fixture, `exam_post_sitting_interval_MonFri_FLSat_fortnightly`, after
the last existing one. Every other byte of the file is untouched; the splice was
verified by re-parsing the result and asserting the other 13 fixtures compare
equal.

It is the first fixture that can tell the post-exam anchor
(`last_exam_date + interval_weeks x 7`) from the setup anchor: the real oracle
places 2026-10-03, an oracle with the branch deleted places 2026-09-26. Verified
byte-exact against the live PL/pgSQL on PostgreSQL 17.11, with
calendar_validate_plan accepting both generators.

Rationale, provenance and the surrounding branch-coverage census:
docs/plans/Calendar_Rule_Branch_Coverage_Census.md

